---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: sites.entries
  size: 1
  alias: entry
permalink: "/site/{{ entry.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ entry.displayUrl }}"
---

<article class="detail">

{#
	One screenshot per site page, from 11ty's service. Deliberately not on the
	leaderboards: those run to a thousand rows, and a thousand screenshot
	requests is not a page, it is a load test pointed at someone else's server.

	Only above a performance score of 75, and only once there is a measurement.
	The service renders the page on a timer, so the slower the site the more
	likely the capture is of a half-drawn or empty page — a picture of our own
	screenshot timeout rather than of the site. Below the threshold there is
	nothing worth showing and a request not worth making.

	Lazy, and sized in the markup so the text beside it does not jump when the
	image lands. Decorative rather than described: what the site looks like is
	not information this page is making a claim about, and "screenshot of
	example.com" read aloud tells you nothing you did not just hear from the
	heading above it.
#}
{% set SCREENSHOT_MIN_PERFORMANCE = 75 %}
{% set screenshot = "" %}
{% if entry.latest.lab.scores.performance >= SCREENSHOT_MIN_PERFORMANCE %}
	{% set screenshot = entry.url | screenshot(meta.screenshotService) %}
{% endif %}

<header class="detail-head{{ ' has-shot' if screenshot }}">
	<div class="detail-head-text">
	<h2 class="page-hed">{{ entry.displayUrl }}</h2>
	<p class="detail-url"><a href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.url }}</a></p>
	<p class="data-age {{ 'stale-age' if entry.dataStale }}">
		{% if entry.latest %}
			Data from {{ entry.latest.date | date("long") }} — <strong>{{ entry.latest.date | since }} old</strong>
			{%- if entry.dataStale %}, older than the {{ sites.coverage.staleAfterHours }}h freshness target{% endif %}.
		{% else %}
			No successful measurement yet.
		{% endif %}
	</p>
	<p class="muted">
		{% for g in entry.groups %}<a href="/group/{{ g }}/">{{ entry.groupNames[loop.index0] }}</a>{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %} ·
		{{ entry.totalCount }} measurement{{ "s" if entry.totalCount != 1 }}
		{% if entry.windowed %}<span title="The report charts the most recent {{ entry.historyCount }}; the rest stay on disk">(charting last {{ entry.historyCount }})</span>{% endif %}
		{% if entry.firstMeasured %}· since {{ entry.firstMeasured | date }}{% endif %}
		{% if entry.lastMeasured %}· last attempt {{ entry.lastMeasured | since }}{% endif %}
	</p>
	</div>
	{#
		After the text, not before it: the heading is what the page is about and
		should come first to a screen reader, and this way the source order and
		the stacked mobile order are the same thing.
	#}
	{% if screenshot %}
	{#
		Hidden from assistive technology and out of the tab order: this is the
		same destination as the URL linked in text directly beside it, and a
		second link to it would be a duplicate to read past and a duplicate to
		tab through. Removing it costs a screen reader nothing — the link is
		still there, in words.
	#}
	<a class="detail-shot-link" href="{{ entry.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
		<img class="detail-shot" src="{{ screenshot }}" width="650" height="650"
			alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
	</a>
	{% endif %}
</header>

{% if entry.stale and entry.latest %}
<div class="notice notice-warn">
	<strong>This data is {{ entry.latest.date | since }} old.</strong>
	<p>
		Sites are measured on a rolling schedule, so figures here are the newest
		successful measurement rather than a reading taken just now. Comparisons
		against other sites may span different points in time.
	</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.redirectTo %}
<div class="notice notice-warn">
	<strong>This URL redirects to <code>{{ entry.redirectTo }}</code>.</strong>
	<p>
		Lighthouse follows the redirect, so the numbers below describe the
		<em>destination</em> page, not this one.
		{% if entry.redirectConfirmed %}
		The move is confirmed, so measurement has already followed it — no config
		change needed, and the history came along.
		{% elif entry.redirectReason == "temporary" %}
		The redirect is temporary (302/303/307), so it is treated as a detour
		rather than a move and history stays here.
		{% elif entry.redirectReason == "unstable" %}
		The destination has not been consistent across recent runs — that pattern
		usually means an A/B test or a geo split rather than a move.
		{% else %}
		Not yet confirmed as a move; it needs to lead to the same place on
		several consecutive runs first.
		{% endif %}
	</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.canonicalUrl and not entry.redirectTo %}
<div class="notice notice-info">
	<strong>This URL redirects to <code>{{ entry.canonicalUrl }}</code>.</strong>
	<p>
		A trailing slash only, so both forms are treated as one site rather than
		two — one history, measured once. Lighthouse follows the redirect, so the
		numbers below describe the canonical page; the only cost is an extra hop
		on each run.
	</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.movedFrom %}
<div class="notice notice-info">
	<strong>Moved from <code>{{ entry.movedFrom }}</code>.</strong>
	<p>
		History from the previous URL is included below{% if entry.moveAt %}, with the
		move on {{ entry.moveAt | date }}{% endif %}. A step-change around that point is
		likely the change of address rather than a regression.
	</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.currentlyFailing %}
<div class="notice notice-error">
	<strong>
		The most recent attempt failed{% if entry.consecutiveFailures > 1 %} ({{ entry.consecutiveFailures }} in a row){% endif %}.
	</strong>
	<code>{{ entry.lastError }}</code>
	{% if entry.latest %}
	<p>Numbers below are from the last successful run, {{ entry.latest.date | since }} old.</p>
	{% else %}
	<p>There is no successful measurement for this site yet.</p>
	{% endif %}
	{% if entry.consecutiveFailures > 2 %}
	<p class="small">Retries are backing off, so this site is being attempted less often than the rest.</p>
	{% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.environmentDrift and entry.environmentDrift.suspect %}
<div class="notice notice-warn">
	<strong>The measuring machine was {{ entry.environmentDrift.direction }} than usual.</strong>
	<p>
		Lighthouse benchmark index was {{ entry.environmentDrift.current }} against a
		baseline of {{ entry.environmentDrift.baseline }}
		({{ entry.environmentDrift.ratio * 100 | round }}%). CPU-bound metrics — TBT,
		TTI, main thread work — are affected by this and may have moved without the
		site changing at all.
	</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if not entry.latest %}
<div class="empty"><p>No successful measurements recorded for this site yet.</p></div>
{% else %}

{% if entry.generator or entry.host %}
<section class="panel">
	<h2>Stack</h2>
	<p class="muted small">
		Detected on the same page load as the accessibility pass — the generator
		from <code>&lt;meta name="generator"&gt;</code> or the shape of the page,
		the host from response headers.
	</p>
	<div class="stack-list">
		{% if entry.generator %}
		<div class="stack-item">
			{% stackIcon entry.generator, 24 %}
			<span>
				<span class="stack-label block">Built with</span>
				{{ entry.generator.name }}{% if entry.generator.version %} {{ entry.generator.version }}{% endif %}
			</span>
		</div>
		{% endif %}
		{% if entry.host %}
		<div class="stack-item">
			{% stackIcon entry.host, 24 %}
			<span>
				<span class="stack-label block">Hosted by</span>
				{{ entry.host.name }}
			</span>
		</div>
		{% endif %}
	</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.cwv %}
<section class="panel">
	<h2>
		Core Web Vitals
		{% if entry.cwv.source == "lab" %}
		<span class="tag">lab approximation</span>
		{% else %}
		<span class="tag">field data{% if entry.cwv.period.scope %}, {{ entry.cwv.period.scope }}-level{% endif %}</span>
		{% endif %}
	</h2>

	{% if entry.cwv.source == "lab" %}
	<p class="muted small">
		No Chrome UX Report data for this URL, so this is a lab approximation using
		TBT in place of INP. Lighthouse cannot measure INP in a lab run — only real
		users produce it.
	</p>
	{% else %}
	<p class="muted small">
		Real Chrome users, 28-day window
		{%- if entry.cwv.period.first %} ({{ entry.cwv.period.first }} → {{ entry.cwv.period.last }}){% endif %}.
		{% if entry.cwv.source == "field-history" %}
		From the backfilled CrUX history rather than this measurement, which predates the API key.
		{% endif %}
		This is what Google measures you on.
	</p>
	{% endif %}
	<div class="cwv">
		{% for part in entry.cwv.parts %}
		<div class="cwv-item cwv-{{ part.rating | ratingClass }}">
			<span class="cwv-key">{{ part.key | upper }}{% if part.proxyFor %} <span class="tag">for {{ part.proxyFor | upper }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
			<span class="cwv-value">{{ part.value | unit("ms" if part.key != "cls" else "") }}</span>
			<span class="cwv-rating">{{ part.rating or "no data" }}</span>
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Scores</h2>
	<div class="cards">
		{% for score in metrics.SCORES %}
		{% set t = entry.trends[score.key] %}
		{% set value = entry.latest.lab.scores[score.key] %}
		<div class="card">
			<div class="card-value score-{{ value | scoreClass }}">{{ value if value != null else "—" }}</div>
			<div class="card-label">{{ score.label }}</div>
			{% if t %}
			<div class="card-spark">{% sparkline t %}</div>
			{% if t.vsPrevious and not t.vsPrevious.unchanged %}
			<div class="card-delta {{ t.vsPrevious | deltaClass }}">
				{{ t.vsPrevious | deltaArrow }} {{ t.vsPrevious | deltaText }}
			</div>
			{% else %}
			<div class="card-delta flat">no change</div>
			{% endif %}
			{% endif %}
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
</section>

{% macro trendtable(rows, entryData, prefix="") %}
<div class="table-scroll">
<table class="grid">
	<thead>
		<tr>
			<th class="col-site">Metric</th>
			<th>Current</th>
			<th>Previous</th>
			<th>Change</th>
			<th>Best</th>
			<th>Worst</th>
			<th class="col-trend">Trend</th>
		</tr>
	</thead>
	<tbody>
	{% for row in rows %}
	{% set t = entryData.trends[prefix + row.key] %}
	{% if t %}
		<tr>
			<td class="col-site">
				<strong>{{ row.label }}</strong>
				{% if row.note %}<span class="muted small block">{{ row.note }}</span>{% endif %}
			</td>
			<td class="num">{{ t.current | unit(row.unit) }}</td>
			<td class="num muted">{{ t.previous | unit(row.unit) }}</td>
			<td class="num {{ t.vsPrevious | deltaClass }}">
				{% if t.vsPrevious %}{{ t.vsPrevious | deltaArrow }} {{ t.vsPrevious | deltaText(row.unit) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}
				{% if t.significant %}<span class="badge badge-sig" title="Larger than this metric's normal run-to-run noise">significant</span>{% endif %}
			</td>
			<td class="num muted">{{ (t.min if t.lowerIsBetter else t.max) | unit(row.unit) }}</td>
			<td class="num muted">{{ (t.max if t.lowerIsBetter else t.min) | unit(row.unit) }}</td>
			<td class="col-trend">{% sparkline t %}</td>
		</tr>
	{% endif %}
	{% endfor %}
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Lab metrics <span class="tag">Lighthouse, {{ entry.latest.formFactor }}</span></h2>
	{{ trendtable(metrics.LAB_METRICS, entry) }}

	{% if entry.latest.lab.lcpBreakdown %}
	<h3>What LCP is made of</h3>
	<p class="muted small">
		A flat LCP number tells you something regressed. The subparts tell you
		whether it was the server, resource discovery, the download, or rendering.
	</p>
	<div class="breakdown">
		{% set lcpMax = entry.latest.lab.lcpBreakdown | sortByValue | maxValue("value") %}
		{% for part in entry.latest.lab.lcpBreakdown | sortByValue %}
		<div class="breakdown-row">
			<span class="breakdown-label breakdown-key">{{ part.key | humanize }}</span>
			{% bar part.value, lcpMax, "warn" %}
			<span class="breakdown-value">{{ part.value | ms }}</span>
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
	{% endif %}
</section>

{% if entry.latest.field %}
<section class="panel">
	<h2>
		Field data <span class="tag">Chrome UX Report, {{ entry.latest.field.scope }}-level</span>
	</h2>
	<p class="muted small">
		Real Chrome users, 28-day trailing window
		({{ entry.latest.field.collectionPeriod.first }} → {{ entry.latest.field.collectionPeriod.last }}).
		This is what Google measures you on.
	</p>

	<div class="table-scroll">
	<table class="grid">
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th class="col-site">Metric</th>
				<th>p75</th>
				<th>Rating</th>
				<th class="col-dist">Distribution (good / needs work / poor)</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
		{% for row in metrics.FIELD_METRICS %}
		{% set m = entry.latest.field.metrics[row.key] %}
		{% if m %}
			<tr>
				<td class="col-site">
					<strong>{{ row.label }}</strong>
					{% if row.coreWebVital %}<span class="badge badge-cwv">CWV</span>{% endif %}
					{% if row.note %}<span class="muted small block">{{ row.note }}</span>{% endif %}
				</td>
				<td class="num">{{ m.p75 | unit(row.unit) }}</td>
				<td><span class="pill pill-{{ m.rating | ratingClass }}">{{ m.rating or "—" }}</span></td>
				<td class="col-dist">
					{% if m.distribution %}
					<span class="dist" title="{{ m.distribution.good }}% good, {{ m.distribution.needsImprovement }}% needs improvement, {{ m.distribution.poor }}% poor">
						<span class="dist-good" style="width:{{ m.distribution.good }}%"></span>
						<span class="dist-avg" style="width:{{ m.distribution.needsImprovement }}%"></span>
						<span class="dist-poor" style="width:{{ m.distribution.poor }}%"></span>
					</span>
					<span class="muted small">{{ m.distribution.good }}% good</span>
					{% else %}—{% endif %}
				</td>
			</tr>
		{% endif %}
		{% endfor %}
		</tbody>
	</table>
	</div>

	{% if entry.labVsField %}
	<h3>Lab vs field</h3>
	<p class="muted small">
		Lab LCP {{ entry.labVsField.lab | ms }} · field p75 {{ entry.labVsField.field | ms }} ·
		real users are <strong>{{ entry.labVsField.ratio }}×</strong>
		{{ "slower" if entry.labVsField.fieldWorse else "faster" }} than the lab.
		{% if entry.labVsField.fieldWorse and entry.labVsField.ratio > 1.5 %}
		A gap this wide usually means real users are on slower devices or networks
		than the simulated ones — the lab number is flattering you.
		{% endif %}
	</p>
	{% endif %}
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if entry.fieldHistory and entry.fieldHistory.series.length %}
<section class="panel">
	<h2>Field history <span class="tag">{{ entry.fieldHistory.series.length }} weeks</span></h2>
	<p class="muted small">
		Weekly p75 from the CrUX History API, backfilled in a single request.
	</p>
	<div class="table-scroll">
	<table class="grid compact">
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th class="col-site">Week ending</th>
				<th>LCP</th><th>INP</th><th>CLS</th><th>FCP</th><th>TTFB</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
		{% for point in entry.fieldHistory.series | reverse | limit(12) %}
			<tr>
				<td class="col-site muted">{{ point.date }}</td>
				{% for key in ["lcp", "inp", "cls", "fcp", "ttfb"] %}
				{% set m = point.metrics[key] %}
				<td class="num"><span class="pill pill-{{ m.rating | ratingClass }}">{{ m.p75 | unit("" if key == "cls" else "ms") }}</span></td>
				{% endfor %}
			</tr>
		{% endfor %}
		</tbody>
	</table>
	</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Page weight</h2>
	{{ trendtable(metrics.WEIGHT_METRICS, entry) }}

	<h3>By resource type</h3>
	<div class="breakdown">
		{% set types = [] %}
		{% for key, val in entry.latest.lab.weight.byType %}
			{% if key != "total" and val.bytes %}{% set types = (types.push({key: key, value: val.bytes, requests: val.requests}), types) %}{% endif %}
		{% endfor %}
		{% set typeMax = types | maxValue("value") %}
		{% for t in types %}
		<div class="breakdown-row">
			<span class="breakdown-label breakdown-key">{{ t.key | humanize }}</span>
			{% bar t.value, typeMax, "neutral" %}
			<span class="breakdown-value">{{ t.value | bytes }} <span class="muted">· {{ t.requests }} req</span></span>
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>

	{% if entry.latest.lab.thirdParty and entry.latest.lab.thirdParty.count %}
	<h3>Third parties <span class="tag">{{ entry.latest.lab.thirdParty.count }} entities</span></h3>
	<p class="muted small">
		{{ entry.latest.lab.thirdParty.bytes | bytes }} transferred,
		{{ entry.latest.lab.thirdParty.mainThreadMs | ms }} of main thread time.
		This is the number most likely to regress without anyone on your team
		shipping anything.
	</p>
	<div class="breakdown">
		{% set tpMax = entry.latest.lab.thirdParty.top | maxValue("bytes") %}
		{% for tp in entry.latest.lab.thirdParty.top %}
		<div class="breakdown-row">
			<span class="breakdown-label">{{ tp.entity }}</span>
			{% bar tp.bytes, tpMax, "warn" %}
			<span class="breakdown-value">{{ tp.bytes | bytes }} <span class="muted">· {{ tp.mainThreadMs | ms }} CPU</span></span>
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
	{% endif %}
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Page health</h2>
	{{ trendtable(metrics.HEALTH_METRICS, entry) }}

	{% if entry.latest.lab.mainThread and entry.latest.lab.mainThread.byGroup %}
	<h3>Main thread work</h3>
	<div class="breakdown">
		{% set mtMax = entry.latest.lab.mainThread.byGroup | sortByValue | maxValue("value") %}
		{% for part in entry.latest.lab.mainThread.byGroup | sortByValue %}
		<div class="breakdown-row">
			<span class="breakdown-label breakdown-key">{{ part.key | humanize }}</span>
			{% bar part.value, mtMax, "neutral" %}
			<span class="breakdown-value">{{ part.value | ms }}</span>
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
	{% endif %}

	{% if entry.axe %}
	<h3>
		Axe violations
		<span class="tag">axe-core {{ entry.axe.version }}, full rule set</span>
	</h3>
	{% if entry.axe.error %}
	<p class="muted small">The axe run failed: <code>{{ entry.axe.error }}</code></p>
	{% else %}
	<p class="muted small">
		<strong>{{ entry.axe.violations }}</strong> violating node{{ "s" if entry.axe.violations != 1 }}
		across {{ entry.axe.violationRules }} rule{{ "s" if entry.axe.violationRules != 1 }},
		{{ entry.axe.passes }} passing. This is a standalone axe run, stricter than the
		subset Lighthouse folds into its score above — and it is the second tiebreaker
		in the ranking.
	</p>
	{% if entry.axe.top.length %}
	<ul class="failures">
		{% for v in entry.axe.top %}
		<li>
			<span class="badge badge-{{ 'error' if v.impact == 'critical' or v.impact == 'serious' else 'stale' }}">{{ v.impact }}</span>
			<code>{{ v.id }}</code> — {{ v.help }}
			<span class="badge">{{ v.nodes }} node{{ "s" if v.nodes != 1 }}</span>
		</li>
		{% endfor %}
	</ul>
	{% endif %}
	{% endif %}
	{% endif %}

	{% if entry.latest.lab.accessibility.failing.length %}
	<h3>Accessibility failures <span class="tag">{{ entry.latest.lab.accessibility.failingCount }} of {{ entry.latest.lab.accessibility.applicableCount }} audits</span></h3>
	<p class="muted small">
		Tracked as a count, not just the score — the weighted score is coarse
		enough that you can ship a broken component and barely move it.
	</p>
	<ul class="failures">
		{% for fail in entry.latest.lab.accessibility.failing %}
		<li>
			<code>{{ fail.id }}</code> — {{ fail.title }}
			{% if fail.nodes %}<span class="badge">{{ fail.nodes }} node{{ "s" if fail.nodes != 1 }}</span>{% endif %}
		</li>
		{% endfor %}
	</ul>
	{% endif %}
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Hygiene</h2>
	<p class="muted small">Changes rarely — which is exactly why a change is worth noticing.</p>
	<div class="chips">
		{% set h = entry.latest.lab.hygiene %}
		{% for check in [
			{k: "https", label: "HTTPS"},
			{k: "hsts", label: "HSTS"},
			{k: "csp", label: "CSP"},
			{k: "clickjacking", label: "Clickjacking protection"},
			{k: "originIsolation", label: "Origin isolation"},
			{k: "trustedTypes", label: "Trusted Types"},
			{k: "bfCache", label: "bfcache"}
		] %}
		<span class="chip chip-{{ 'good' if h[check.k] == 1 else ('poor' if h[check.k] == 0 else 'none') }}">
			{{ check.label }}
		</span>
		{% endfor %}
		<span class="chip chip-none">{{ h.protocol or "—" }}</span>
		{% if h.consoleErrors %}<span class="chip chip-poor">{{ h.consoleErrors }} console error{{ "s" if h.consoleErrors != 1 }}</span>{% endif %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Measurement log</h2>
	<p class="muted small">
		Every stored run for this URL, newest first. Failures are kept as records —
		"this site was down on Tuesday" is data too.
	</p>
	<div class="table-scroll">
	<table class="grid compact">
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th class="col-site">When</th>
				<th>Perf</th><th>LCP</th><th>CLS</th><th>TBT</th><th>Weight</th>
				<th>Runs</th><th>Spread</th><th>Bench</th><th>Took</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
		{% for point in entry.history | reverse | limit(30) %}
			<tr{% if point.error %} class="row-failing"{% endif %}>
				<td class="col-site">
					{{ point.date | date("long") }}
					{% if entry.movedFrom and point.via != entry.url %}
					<span class="badge" title="Measured at {{ point.via }}, before the move">old URL</span>
					{% endif %}
				</td>
				{% if point.error %}
					<td colspan="8" class="muted"><code>{{ point.error }}</code></td>
					<td class="num muted">{{ (point.durationMs / 1000) | round(1) }}s</td>
				{% else %}
					<td class="score score-{{ point.performance | scoreClass }}">{{ point.performance }}</td>
					<td class="num">{{ point.lcp | ms }}</td>
					<td class="num">{{ point.cls | unit("") }}</td>
					<td class="num">{{ point.tbt | ms }}</td>
					<td class="num">{{ point.total | bytes }}</td>
					<td class="num muted">{{ point.completedRuns }}/{{ point.requestedRuns }}</td>
					<td class="num muted">{{ ("±" + point.spread) if point.spread != null else "—" }}</td>
					<td class="num muted" title="Lighthouse benchmark index of the measuring machine">{{ point.bench | num }}</td>
					<td class="num muted">{{ (point.durationMs / 1000) | round(1) }}s</td>
				{% endif %}
			</tr>
		{% endfor %}
		</tbody>
	</table>
	</div>
</section>

{% endif %}

<section class="panel">
	<h2>Embed this score</h2>
	<p class="muted small">
		Live below, then the markup that produces it. Drop that on any page to show
		{{ entry.displayUrl }}'s scores, updated whenever this instance
		re-measures — <a href="/embed/">more about the component</a>. <em>Don’t forget to bundle the <code>speedlify-score.js</code> component code into your site!</em>
	</p>
	{#
		The live one and the snippet resolve their instance URL differently, and
		the difference is the point.

		This example runs on this site, so htmlBaseUrl — the same base every other
		link here uses, correct whether served from a subdirectory or a root.

		The snippet below gets pasted onto a *different* site, where a path like
		/speedlify2/ would resolve against that site's domain. It needs the
		absolute URL, which is meta.url.
	#}
	<script type="module" src="/js/speedlify-score.js"></script>
	<p class="embed-live">
		<speedlify-score speedlify-url="{{ '/' | htmlBaseUrl }}" url="{{ entry.url }}"></speedlify-score>
	</p>

	<pre><code>&lt;speedlify-score speedlify-url="{{ meta.url }}/" url="{{ entry.url }}"&gt;&lt;/speedlify-score&gt;</code></pre>
</section>

</article>
